# Sky whale body plan — HUMPBACK variant. A candidate alongside
# ships/whale.ship (the flat-backed sperm-whale profile); same format,
# same block vocabulary, different silhouette. Preview it without
# booting the game:
#
#   godot --headless --path . --script tools/ship_preview.gd -- ships/whale_humpback.ship
#
#   W  blubber (buoyant flesh — keep it the majority or the whale falls)
#   M  meat (dense core)
#
# Theme: an arched-back gentle giant. Read right-to-left, the profile is
# a blunt stub of a head (shorter than the sperm whale's ram), a deep
# rounded chest that sags to the lowest row, then the whole midsection
# rides UP into the hump — the dorsal line climbs from row 2 at the tail
# strand to row 0 amidships and settles back to row 1 over the head, so
# the top edge visibly rises and falls. The tail thins to a 2-row strand
# and ends in a broad two-pronged fluke: two 2x2 blades split by the
# strand's own centreline.
#
# Proportions follow the owner's survey (2026-08-20): thin parts run 2
# rows (the tail strand), thickest 4 rows, and no column ever carries
# more than 4 body cells — including the notched fluke columns, which
# hold 2 cells per blade.
#
# The two empty cells in the head-side core are the STOMACH cavity —
# fully enclosed on all four orthogonal sides (meat above, meat left and
# right, blubber below), so mining in breaks through into a hollow.
#
# Meat is an inner core only: every M cell has body on all four sides
# and never touches the silhouette. Blubber is 59 of 78 cells (76%),
# which is what keeps the carcass in the air.

# HEADERS (2026-09-05) — what this file already was, said out loud, so the
# drafting table can file it. Header lines only: the grid below is untouched.
name Humpback Whale
kind whale

origin 12 2

WW..........WWWWW........
WWW........WMMMMMWWWWWW..
..WWWWWWWWWMMMMMMMMMMMWWW
..WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWM..MMWWW
WWW..............WWWWWWW.
WW.......................
